# Mark the moment (#551; written before the implementation): on the simulated Index, both thumbstick clicks held
# together for 3 s write a marker folder <user dir>\marks\<utc>-<n>\ (left.png, right.png, recorder.txt, clip.vrsim,
# meta.txt; note.wav when the voice note is on and a microphone recorded one) and show "Moment marked (#N)" in the
# hero-dialogue panel (the subtitle panel of #460 / D-055) for about 2 s. Held 2.5 s and let go: no mark. Held on
# after the mark: no second mark until they are let go. The hold no longer opens the game menu (the D-058 fallback is
# gone; menu-long-press.xrs has the radial's way to it). The feature's one CI sequence (coordinator Tests and CI
# rule 11), about 15 s after the load.
#
# Assumes (the worker adds them, named exactly; tests/vr/MarkMomentTest.h has the whole interface):
#   marks.count          (count)  marks written since the start
#   marks.last           (text)   the last mark's folder name: <yyyymmdd>T<hhmmss>Z-<n> (UTC, n = its number)
#   marks.lastFiles      (text)   the non-empty files in it, sorted by name, joined by "," without spaces
#   marks.recording      (bool)   a voice note records now
#   marks.note           (bool)   the voice note is on (cfg.ini vr_mark_note; the channel's `marks note on|off`)
#   marks.holdMs         (number) the hold: 3000
#   scene.subtitle.notice (text)  the notice the hero-dialogue panel shows: none | marked | recording
#   log "[vr] mark #<n>: marks\<folder> files=<lastFiles>" once the folder is written, and the panel's
#   "vr.scene.subtitle notice=marked ... text="Moment marked (#<n>)"" when the confirmation shows
# The voice note is turned off for the run: CI runs on the owner's PC, where a microphone may be plugged in (a room
# recording must never land in a CI user directory); the note itself is a host test (tests/vr/VoiceNoteTest.h) and
# the owner's headset test.
@sim idle
@save mvp-new-game
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.input.controllers eq index
@assert menuMode eq ingame
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert marks.holdMs eq 3000
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq none
marks note off
@frames 2
@assert marks.note eq false

# 1. Both stick clicks held 2.5 s and let go: no mark (and no game menu, the old fallback's 2 s are long past)
vr-input down left.stick_click; vr-input down right.stick_click
@wait 2500
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert menuMode eq ingame
vr-input up left.stick_click; vr-input up right.stick_click
@wait 500
@assert marks.count eq 0
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq none
@assert menuMode eq ingame

# 2. Held 3 s: the mark, its confirmation in the hero-dialogue panel (below the view centre: the hero's panel)
@mark
vr-input down left.stick_click; vr-input down right.stick_click
@wait 2000
@assert marks.count eq 0
@until marks.count eq 1 3s
@until scene.subtitle.notice eq marked 1s
@assert scene.subtitle.visible eq true
@assert scene.subtitle.drawn eq chest
@assert marks.recording eq false
@assert menuMode eq ingame

# 3. Still held: the confirmation stays about 2 s and goes; no second mark while they are held (3 s past the mark)
@wait 1000
@assert scene.subtitle.notice eq marked
@assert scene.subtitle.panel eq true
@until scene.subtitle.notice eq none 2s
@wait 2000
@assert marks.count eq 1
vr-input up left.stick_click; vr-input up right.stick_click
@wait 500
@assert marks.count eq 1
@assert menuMode eq ingame

# 4. The folder: the five files, written and not empty; no voice note (off). The log has the confirmation's line and
# the folder's, in either order (the files may be written after the confirmation shows): one look-ahead for each
@until marks.lastFiles eq clip.vrsim,left.png,meta.txt,recorder.txt,right.png 10s
@assert marks.recording eq false
@log (?s)^(?=.*vr\.scene\.subtitle notice=marked [^\n]*text="Moment marked \(#1\)")(?=.*\[vr\] mark #1: marks\\\d{8}T\d{6}Z-1 files=clip\.vrsim,left\.png,meta\.txt,recorder\.txt,right\.png) 5s

marks note on
@frames 2
@assert marks.note eq true
@assert errors eq 0
